description:
A shareable OpenSearch <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/token-filters/synonym-graph/'>synonym_graph</a> (or legacy <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/token-filters/synonym/'>synonym</a>) token filter. SynonymSets belong to an Organization; the qualified name '{organizationName}-{name}' is what a SearchConfiguration references in its 'synonymSets' list to bring this filter into the index. SynonymSets are injected into analyzers at the 'synapse_synonyms' placeholder position in 'indexFilterOrder' / 'searchFilterOrder' — see TextAnalyzerSettings for the rule.

A small example using OpenSearch native synonym syntax — 'a, b, c' for equivalent (bidirectional) and 'a, b => c, d' for explicit (directional) expansion:

  {
    "organizationName": "biomed",
    "name": "medical_terms",
    "definition": "{\"type\":\"synonym_graph\",\"synonyms\":[\"tumor, neoplasm, cancer\",\"AD => Alzheimer's disease\"]}"
  }

Tuning suggestions:

  // Multi-word synonyms — prefer synonym_graph (it handles phrases correctly):
  "definition": "{\"type\":\"synonym_graph\",\"synonyms\":[\"new york city, NYC, nyc\"]}"

  // Disable bidirectional expansion (only the LHS is treated as a synonym source):
  "definition": "{\"type\":\"synonym_graph\",\"synonyms\":[...], \"expand\":false}"

  // Tolerate malformed rule lines without failing the whole filter:
  "definition": "{\"type\":\"synonym_graph\",\"synonyms\":[...], \"lenient\":true}"

Cannot be deleted while any persisted resource references it. See the OpenSearch <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/token-filters/synonym-graph/'>synonym_graph filter docs</a> for the full parameter list (synonyms, format, expand, lenient, etc.).
